  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1010 PM CDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\nThe long term should remain fairly tranquil under the influence of \nan upper level ridge and subsequent sfc high pressure from the north.\nHighs during this time are forecast to continue to reach the 90s \nwith heat indices up to 100 degrees, which will keep us without any \nheat products on the table. One thing to watch will be a shortwave \nand subsequent sfc low with an accompanying frontal boundary that may\nclip the western portion of our area on Monday into Tuesday. For \nnow, have kept PoPs aligned with blended guidance due to uncertainty \nin the evolution and speed of this front. Therefore, low chances (20%\nor less) of rain exists Monday into Tuesday. If you have outdoor \ninterests early next week, be sure to check back in for forecast \nupdates.",
